\ Strict-mode compilation of `times`: the recursive loop combinator's word body
\ calls `2dip` on its quotation parameter, collapsing the abstract stack to a
\ bounded row. The preserved-bounded-row layout keeps the counter and quotation
\ live above that row, so the body compiles to native C and the build succeeds
\ under --interpreter-fallback=false (the quotation parameter still runs through
\ the interpreter). The call site runs the inlined counter loop.
3 [ "tick" print-line ] times
